<figure class="migration-race" aria-labelledby="r22-race-title" data-migration-race>
  <figcaption id="r22-race-title"><span>Figure 1</span> A row can change after the backfill reads it</figcaption>
  <fieldset><legend>Write protocol</legend><label><input type="radio" name="r22-protocol" value="saved" checked /> Saved copy</label><label><input type="radio" name="r22-protocol" value="bridge" /> Decimal bridge</label></fieldset>
  <div class="race-scene">
    <div class="worker"><strong>Backfill</strong><p data-live data-worker>No value read yet</p></div>
    <div class="pair"><strong>Order 103 · line 1</strong><div class="columns"><div><code>unit_price</code><b data-live data-decimal>20.00</b></div><div><code>unit_price_minor</code><b data-live data-minor>NULL</b></div></div><p data-live data-invariant>New representation missing</p></div>
    <div class="writer"><strong>Old caller</strong><p data-live data-writer>Writes decimal prices only</p></div>
  </div>
  <p data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">The scratch row starts at 20.00 with no minor-unit value. Step through a competing edit.</p>
  <div class="controls" role="group" aria-label="Backfill race playback"><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back>Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 4</span><span data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></span></div>
  <details><summary>All steps as text</summary><p>Both schedules start with 20.00 and NULL. The backfill reads 2000. An old caller then changes the decimal to 21.00. Without a bridge, copying the saved 2000 leaves 21.00 and 2000. With the decimal bridge, the caller’s write also stores 2100; a backfill restricted to missing values leaves that correct pair alone.</p></details>
  <p class="caption">An illustrative scratch edit, separate from the fixed purchase history. The bridge derives the minor value from the decimal in the same row write. It does not make two independent writes atomic.</p>
</figure>
<script>
import { stepper } from '../../figures/stepper.mjs';
for (const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-migration-race]')) {
 const el = (s:string) => root.querySelector<HTMLElement>(s)!;
 const safe = () => root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('input:checked')!.value === 'bridge';
 const explain = [
 'The scratch row starts at 20.00 with no minor-unit value. Step through a competing edit.',
 'The backfill reads 20.00 and calculates 2000. That saved value describes the row it read, not every future version.',
 '', ''
 ];
 const player = stepper(root,{steps:()=>4,draw:(step:number)=>{
  const bridge=safe();
  el('[data-decimal]').textContent=step<2?'20.00':'21.00';
  el('[data-minor]').textContent=step<2?'NULL':bridge?'2100':step===2?'NULL':'2000';
  el('[data-worker]').textContent=step===0?'No value read yet':step<3?'Saved calculation: 2000':bridge?'Missing-only write skips this row':'Writes the saved 2000';
  el('[data-writer]').textContent=step<2?'Writes decimal prices only':bridge?'Writes 21.00; bridge derives 2100':'Writes 21.00; minor value left missing';
  el('[data-invariant]').textContent=step<2?'New representation missing':bridge?'Equivalent: 21.00 × 100 = 2100':step===2?'New representation missing':'Mismatch: 21.00 × 100 ≠ 2000';
  el('[data-explanation]').textContent=step<2?explain[step]:step===2?(bridge?'The old caller writes 21.00. The trigger stores 2100 as part of that same write.':'The old caller writes 21.00 after the backfill read. No bridge fills the new column.'):(bridge?'The missing-only backfill leaves 2100 alone. The pair remains correct, including this competing write.':'The backfill copies its saved calculation. A non-NULL value now exists, but it represents the wrong price.');
 }});
 root.querySelectorAll('input').forEach(input=>input.addEventListener('change',()=>{el('[data-reset]').click();player.render();}));
}
</script>
